# Grok-only models (hard rule)

This cloud environment is locked to **Grok**. No other model family may be used
for any purpose: planning, code, search, screenshots, screen recordings,
video review, browser testing, or any Task / subagent.

## Allowed model slugs

Pass one of these on every `Task` / subagent launch (never omit with the
intent of getting a non-Grok model):

- `inherit` — only when the parent run is already a Grok model
- `cursor-grok-4.6-high`
- `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast`
- `cursor-grok-4.6-medium`
- `cursor-grok-4.6-medium-fast`
- `cursor-grok-4.6-low`
- `cursor-grok-4.6-low-fast`
- `cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh`
- `cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh-fast`

Default: `inherit` if the parent is Grok; otherwise `cursor-grok-4.6-high`.

## Forbidden

Never launch, resume, or route work through:

- Claude (`claude-*`)
- GPT (`gpt-*`)
- Gemini (`gemini-*`)
- Composer (`composer-*`)
- Muse (`muse-*`)
- Any other non-Grok slug

This applies to **all** subagent types, including `computerUse` (screenshots /
manual GUI testing), `videoReview` (walkthrough videos), `explore`,
`generalPurpose`, `bugbot`, `security-review`, `hostinger-deployment-reviewer`,
and any future type.

## If a prompt asks for another model

Stay on Grok. Do not switch. Say that this environment is Grok-only and
continue the work on Grok.
